{"eeg_signals": "EEG signals are electrical recordings of brain activity obtained through electrodes on the scalp. They are essential for diagnosing neurological conditions like epilepsy, monitoring brain function, and detecting abnormalities such as seizures. These signals are analyzed and classified to determine their nature, such as normal, preictal, or seizure states.|Here is another description: EEG signals, or Electroencephalogram signals, are electrical impulses recorded from the brain. They are used in various medical and research applications to monitor brain activity, diagnose neurological conditions, and study brain functions. EEG signals provide valuable data for understanding the electrical patterns associated with different brain states and activities.|Here is another description: EEG signals refer to the electrical activity recorded from the brain using electrodes placed on the scalp. These signals are used to monitor brain activity and can help in diagnosing various neurological conditions."},
