{"a_single_channel_eeg_signal": "A single channel EEG signal is a type of electroencephalogram recording that captures brain activity through a single sensor or electrode, as opposed to multiple channels which use several sensors. In this research, each record is such a single channel signal, lasting 23.6 seconds."},
{"each_record__has_duration_of__23_6_s": "The predicate \"has duration of\" specifies the length or time span of each EEG record. It indicates that each record is measured over a specific period, which is crucial for analyzing the EEG signals and categorizing them into different classes based on the duration and characteristics of the signals."},
