{"normal_dataset": "The normal dataset is a collection of EEG signals specifically categorized as normal, indicating no seizure activity at the time of recording. It is part of a larger dataset used in research to differentiate between normal, preictal, and seizure states in EEG recordings.|Here is another description: The normal dataset is a collection of EEG signals obtained from 5 healthy subjects, used in research to differentiate between normal, preictal, and seizure states."},
