{"preictal_class": "The preictal class is a category within the EEG dataset that includes data from patients who are in a state prior to experiencing a seizure. It is one of three classes in the dataset, alongside normal and seizure classes.|Here is another description: The preictal class represents a state in which an individual is at an increased risk of experiencing a seizure. In the context, it is one of the categories into which EEG signals can be classified. Here, it is noted that some signals were incorrectly classified into this category."},
