{"seizure_class": "The seizure class is a category within the EEG dataset that includes EEG signals from subjects experiencing epileptic seizures. It is one of three classes in the dataset, alongside normal and preictal classes.|Here is another description: The seizure class represents a category of EEG signals that are characteristic of seizure activity in the brain. In the context, 88% of the EEG signals were accurately identified as belonging to this class.|Here is another description: The seizure class represents a category of EEG signals that are characteristic of seizure activity, which is crucial for diagnosing and managing epilepsy and other seizure disorders."},
