{"seizure_class_data": "The seizure class data refers to a specific category within the EEG dataset collected by Andrzejak et al. at Bonn University. This class includes 100 EEG signals, each lasting 23.6 seconds, which were recorded from subjects experiencing epileptic seizures."},
{"seizure_class_data__acquired_when__subjects_were_having_epilepsy": "The predicate \"acquired when\" indicates the specific condition or state during which the seizure class data was collected. In this context, it highlights the timing of the EEG signal acquisition in relation to the subjects' epileptic episodes."},
