{"a_lot_of_attention_in_recent_years": "\"A lot of attention in recent years\" refers to the increased focus and investment in deep learning technologies over the past few years. This surge in attention is driven by the growing recognition of its capabilities in enhancing automation, improving decision-making processes, and enabling innovative solutions across different sectors."},
{"cnn": "CNN, or Convolutional Neural Network, is an advanced type of neural network that has been enhanced for better performance. It is particularly noted for its shift and translational invariance properties, making it highly effective in processing various types of image data.|Here is another description: CNN, or Convolutional Neural Network, is a type of deep learning model that is particularly effective in processing grid-like data such as images and, in this context, physiological signals like ECGs. It is designed to automatically and adaptively learn spatial hierarchies of features from data.|Here is another description: CNN, or Convolutional Neural Network, is a type of deep learning algorithm commonly used in image and signal processing tasks. In the context of physiological signal analysis, CNNs have been explored for their potential in detecting patterns and anomalies within data.|Here is another description: CNN refers to Convolutional Neural Networks, a class of deep learning models commonly used in image and signal processing tasks. In the context provided, CNN is utilized for analyzing physiological signals, specifically ECG signals, to detect arrhythmias."},
