{"the_use_of_cnn_using_physiological_signals": "The use of CNN using physiological signals refers to the application of Convolutional Neural Networks, a class of deep learning algorithms, to process and interpret data derived from physiological measurements such as ECG (electrocardiogram) signals. This involves training the CNN to recognize patterns, detect anomalies, and make predictions based on the physiological data input."},
