{"authors_previous_works__implemented__cnn_on_ecg_signals": "The predicate \"implemented\" indicates that the authors have put into practical use or applied a specific method or technology in their research. In this case, it refers to the application of Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN) to analyze Electrocardiogram (ECG) signals."},
{"cnn_on_ecg_signals": "CNN on ECG signals refers to the use of Convolutional Neural Networks, a class of deep learning models, to process and analyze Electrocardiogram signals. ECG signals are graphical representations of the electrical activity of the heart and are commonly used in the diagnosis of heart conditions."},
{"cnn__was_employed_to__automatically_detect_arrhythmias": "The phrase \"was employed to\" indicates that the CNN model was utilized or applied for a specific purpose. In this case, it was used as a tool or method to achieve a particular goal related to the analysis of ECG signals."},
{"automatically_detect_arrhythmias": "Automatically detecting arrhythmias refers to the process of using a system, in this case, a CNN, to identify abnormal heart rhythms from ECG data without human intervention. This is crucial for timely diagnosis and treatment of heart conditions."},
{"cnn__used__different_intervals_of_tachycardia_ecg_segments": "The predicate \"used\" indicates the application or employment of the CNN algorithm in a specific context or task. In this case, it refers to the utilization of CNN for analyzing and detecting arrhythmias in ECG signals."},
{"different_intervals_of_tachycardia_ecg_segments": "Different intervals of tachycardia ECG segments refer to segments of electrocardiogram (ECG) recordings that exhibit tachycardia, a condition characterized by an abnormally fast heart rate. These segments are used as input data for the CNN algorithm to train and test its effectiveness in detecting arrhythmias."},
{"accuracies": "The accuracies refer to the effectiveness of a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) algorithm in detecting arrhythmias from Electrocardiogram (ECG) signals. These accuracies are specific to the CNN's performance in analyzing tachycardia ECG segments."},
{"accuracies__were__92_5_and_94_9_using_2_s_and_5_s_ecg_segments_respectively": "The predicate \"were\" indicates the measured or achieved level of performance of the CNN algorithm when applied to ECG signals for the detection of arrhythmias. It signifies the result obtained from the implementation of the CNN on different durations of ECG segments."},
{"92_5_and_94_9_using_2_s_and_5_s_ecg_segments_respectively": "The object \"92.5% and 94.9% using 2-s and 5-s ECG segments, respectively\" specifies the exact accuracies achieved by the CNN algorithm. These percentages represent the success rates of the CNN in correctly identifying arrhythmias from ECG signals of two different durations: 2 seconds and 5 seconds."},
{"cnn__was_recently_employed_in__the_automated": "\"Was recently employed in\" indicates that the CNN model has been used or applied in a specific context or task. In this case, it highlights the recent application of CNN in processing and analyzing ECG signals to automatically detect arrhythmias."},
