{"convolution": "Convolution is a mathematical operation used in neural networks, especially in convolutional layers of CNNs, to process input data by applying filters to extract features. It is also used in signal processing for image and audio analysis.|Here is another description: Convolution refers to the process of applying a kernel or filter to a feature map in a neural network, which is a fundamental operation in convolutional neural networks (CNNs). It involves sliding the kernel over the feature map and computing the dot product at each position to produce a new feature map."},
