{"max_pooling__has_padding__2": "The predicate \"has_padding\" indicates that the max-pooling operation includes a padding parameter. Padding is used to add extra layers of zeros around the input matrix to control the spatial dimensions of the output.|Here is another description: The predicate \"has_padding\" indicates that the max-pooling operation includes a padding parameter. Padding is used to add additional layers of zeros around the edge of the input matrix, which can help to preserve the dimensions of the output feature map.|Here is another description: The predicate \"has_padding\" indicates that the max-pooling operation includes a padding parameter. Padding is used to add extra pixels around the border of the input to control the spatial size of the output volume.|Here is another description: The predicate \"has_padding\" indicates that the max-pooling operation includes a padding parameter. Padding is used to add additional layers of zeros around the edge of the input matrix, which can help to preserve the edge information of the input data during the pooling process."},
