{"epilepsy_factsheet__year__2017": "The year predicate indicates the publication or update year of the Epilepsy factsheet, which is crucial for understanding the timeliness and relevance of the information provided within the document."},
{"2017": "The year 2017 is notable for several significant publications and updates across various fields. It marks the last update year of the Epilepsy factsheet by the World Health Organization, ensuring current data on epilepsy. In scientific journals, 2017 saw the publication of contemporary research papers, including a volume of ACI Mater. J., an article in the Korean Journal of Radiology, and several articles in Information Sciences. Notably, U.R. Acharya and colleagues published groundbreaking research on the application of deep convolutional neural networks for detecting myocardial infarction and coronary artery disease through ECG signals, contributing to advancements in medical diagnostics using artificial intelligence. Additionally, a research paper on a deep convolutional neural network model for heartbeat classification was introduced, allowing for its evaluation and potential integration into medical practices.|Here is another description: The year 2017 marks the time when the specific research or publication by Appl. Signal Process. Meth. Syst. Anal. Physiol. Health was made available or completed.|Here is another description: The year 2017 is the specific year in which the referenced work, \"A new approach to characterize epileptic seizures using analytic time-frequency flexible wavelet transform and fractal dimension\" by M. Sharma, R.B. Pachori, and U.R. Acharya, was published in the journal Pattern Recognition Letters."},
{"epilepsy_factsheet__url__http_www_who_int_mediacentre_factsheets_fs999_en": "The 'url' predicate indicates the specific web address where the Epilepsy factsheet can be accessed online, serving as a direct link to the resource for further reading and information."},
