{"seizure__can_cause__changes_in_behavior_movements_feelings_and_levels_of_consciousness": "The phrase \"can cause\" indicates a potential outcome or effect that may result from the occurrence of a seizure."},
{"changes_in_behavior_movements_feelings_and_levels_of_consciousness": "Changes in behavior, movements, feelings, and levels of consciousness are common manifestations that can occur during or after a seizure, reflecting the impact of abnormal brain activity on an individual's physical and mental state."},
{"epilepsy__is__a_condition_characterized_by_recurrent_seizures": "The predicate \"is\" in this context serves as a linking verb to describe the nature or identity of epilepsy, connecting it to its characteristic feature."},
{"a_condition_characterized_by_recurrent_seizures": "A condition characterized by recurrent seizures refers to a state where an individual experiences repeated episodes of seizures, which are sudden, uncontrolled electrical disturbances in the brain."},
{"seizures__can_be__caused_by_various_factors_including_head_injuries_infections_and_genetic_factors": "The phrase \"can be\" indicates a possibility or potential cause-effect relationship, suggesting that seizures may occur as a result of certain conditions or events."},
{"caused_by_various_factors_including_head_injuries_infections_and_genetic_factors": "Various factors such as head injuries, infections, and genetic factors can trigger seizures. Head injuries may damage brain tissue, infections can cause inflammation, and genetic factors may predispose individuals to seizures."},
{"seizure__treatment__may_include_medications_surgery_or_other_therapies": "Treatment for seizures involves a range of medical interventions aimed at controlling or reducing the frequency and severity of seizures. The goal of treatment is to improve the quality of life for individuals affected by seizures."},
{"may_include_medications_surgery_or_other_therapies": "The treatment for seizures may include medications, surgery, or other therapies. Medications are the most common treatment and are designed to prevent seizures from occurring. Surgery may be considered for individuals whose seizures are not controlled by medication, and other therapies can include dietary changes or devices that stimulate the vagus nerve."},
{"international_league_against_epilepsy_ilae": "The International League Against Epilepsy (ILAE) is a global organization dedicated to advancing the understanding, diagnosis, treatment, and prevention of epilepsy. It serves as a platform for collaboration among professionals and researchers in the field of neurology and epilepsy."},
{"international_league_against_epilepsy_ilae__has_website__https_www_epilepsydiagnosis_org": "The predicate \"has_website\" indicates that the International League Against Epilepsy (ILAE) maintains an official online presence. This website serves as a resource for information, updates, and educational materials related to epilepsy."},
