{"s_v_sree": "S.V. Sree is an author who has contributed to scientific literature, particularly in the field of medical signal processing and analysis. Their work is often collaborative, involving multiple co-authors to explore complex topics in depth.|Here is another description: S.V. Sree is a co-author who, alongside U.R. Acharya, has worked on the application of principal component analysis in the field of biomedical engineering. His contributions are integral to the research paper that explores the automatic detection of epileptic EEG activities.|Here is another description: S.V. Sree is a researcher who has contributed to the field of biomedical signal processing, specifically in the analysis of electroencephalogram (EEG) signals for medical diagnostics."},
{"s_v_sree__co_author__automated_eeg_analysis_of_epilepsy_a_review": "The term \"co-author\" signifies a collaborative effort in the creation of a scientific publication. It indicates that S.V. Sree worked alongside other researchers to compile, analyze, and present findings in a comprehensive review."},
