{"a_wavelet_chaos_methodology": "A wavelet-chaos methodology is an innovative approach that combines wavelet analysis with chaos theory to analyze complex signals, such as EEGs. This methodology aims to detect and characterize seizure and epilepsy by examining both the time and frequency domains of the EEG signals, providing a more comprehensive understanding of the underlying neurological activities.|Here is another description: A wavelet-chaos methodology is a sophisticated analytical technique that combines wavelet transform and chaos theory to process and interpret complex signals.|Here is another description: A wavelet-chaos methodology is a scientific approach developed for the analysis of electroencephalogram (EEG) signals and their sub-bands, aimed at detecting seizure and epilepsy."},
