{"sample_normal_interictal_and_seizure_eeg_signals_from_the_bonn_university_database": "The object \"sample normal, interictal, and seizure EEG signals from the Bonn University database\" refers to the specific types of electroencephalogram (EEG) signals that are being shown in Fig. 2. These signals are categorized into normal, interictal (periods between seizures), and seizure activities, and they are sourced from a reputable database at Bonn University, indicating their credibility and relevance for research or diagnostic purposes."},
