{"preictal_class": "The preictal class refers to a category of EEG data collected from epileptic patients who were not experiencing a seizure at the time of recording. This class is part of a larger dataset used in epilepsy research to differentiate between normal, preictal, and seizure states.|Here is another description: The preictal class refers to a category of EEG data collected from epileptic patients who were not experiencing a seizure at the time of recording. This class is part of a larger dataset used for research purposes, which includes normal and seizure classes as well."},
