{"100_data_from_5_epileptic_patients": "The object \"100 data from 5 epileptic patients\" refers to the specific quantity and source of the EEG recordings within the preictal class. It indicates that there are 100 individual EEG signal recordings, each lasting 23.6 seconds, obtained from five different patients who have been diagnosed with epilepsy but were not undergoing a seizure during the recording period."},
{"preictal_class__when__they_did_not_undergo_seizure_during_the_time_of_acquisition": "The predicate \"when\" in this context signifies the temporal condition under which the EEG data for the preictal class was acquired. It indicates that the data was recorded during a specific time frame relative to the occurrence of seizures."},
{"they_did_not_undergo_seizure_during_the_time_of_acquisition": "The object \"they did not undergo seizure during the time of acquisition\" describes the state of the epileptic patients from whom the preictal EEG data was collected. It specifies that these patients were not experiencing a seizure while the EEG signals were being recorded."},
