{"1_d_deep_convolutional_network_cnn": "The 1-D deep convolutional network (CNN) is a type of neural network designed to process one-dimensional data, such as time-series signals. In this context, it is used to analyze the normalized EEG signals for training and testing purposes.|Here is another description: The 1-D deep convolutional network (CNN) is a type of neural network designed specifically for processing one-dimensional data, such as time-series signals. It is structured to automatically and adaptively learn spatial hierarchies of features from input data."},
{"1_d_deep_convolutional_network_cnn__is_used_for__training_and_testing": "The phrase \"is used for\" indicates the purpose or application of the 1-D deep convolutional network (CNN) in this context. It signifies that the CNN is employed as a tool or method to achieve specific tasks related to the input data."},
{"training_and_testing": "Training and testing refer to the two primary phases in the machine learning process. Training involves feeding the network with a set of examples to learn patterns, while testing evaluates the network's performance on unseen data to assess its generalization capability."},
{"sampling_rate": "The sampling rate refers to the frequency at which data points are collected from a continuous signal, in this case, an EEG signal. It is a critical parameter in signal processing as it determines the resolution and quality of the recorded data."},
