{"image_recognition__includes_analysis_of__fundus_images": "The phrase \"includes analysis of\" signifies that the subject, image recognition, encompasses the examination and interpretation of specific types of images. In this context, it highlights the capability of image recognition systems to process and understand particular image types, such as fundus images."},
{"fundus_images": "Fundus images are photographs of the interior surface of the eye, including the retina, optic disc, and blood vessels. These images are crucial in diagnosing various eye conditions and diseases, such as diabetic retinopathy, glaucoma, and age-related macular degeneration. Analyzing fundus images helps medical professionals detect abnormalities and monitor the progression of eye diseases."},
