{"convolution": "Convolution is a mathematical operation used in signal processing and neural networks, especially in convolutional neural networks (CNNs), to process input data by applying filters or kernels to extract features. It is a fundamental operation in convolutional layers, which learn spatial hierarchies of features from input data.|Here is another description: Convolution refers to the mathematical operation applied to the feature map in Layer 8, involving a kernel of size 4. This process is a fundamental step in many neural network architectures, particularly in convolutional neural networks (CNNs), where it helps to extract features from the input data."},
