{"fully_connected_layer": "The fully connected layer is a type of layer in neural networks where each neuron is connected to every neuron in the previous layer. It is typically used after convolutional and pooling layers to perform high-level reasoning using the features extracted by the earlier layers."},
{"fully_connected_layer__has__full_connection_to_all_the_activations_in_the_previous_layer": "The predicate \"has\" in this context indicates the characteristic or property of the fully connected layer. Specifically, it denotes that the layer possesses full connections to all activations in the layer that precedes it."},
