{"prevent_overfitting_of_the_data": "Preventing overfitting of the data is a critical objective in machine learning to ensure that the model generalizes well to unseen data. Overfitting occurs when a model learns the training data too well, including its noise and outliers, which can lead to poor performance on new, unseen data. Lambda helps mitigate this by adding a penalty to the loss function, discouraging overly complex models."},
