{"gaussian_mixture_model_gmm_classifier": "A Gaussian mixture model (GMM) classifier is a probabilistic model that assumes all the data points are generated from a mixture of several Gaussian distributions with unknown parameters. In the context of EEG signal classification, a GMM classifier is used to model the distribution of features extracted from EEG signals and to classify these signals into different categories based on the modeled distributions."},
