{"2017": "The year 2017 was marked by significant publications and updates in various research fields, including health, engineering, and signal processing. Notable contributions included the World Health Organization's fact sheet on epilepsy, advancements in deep learning for concrete strength estimation and cell segmentation, and several studies on automated medical condition detection using convolutional neural networks. Specific highlights were the introduction of a deep convolutional neural network model for heartbeat classification, the application of tunable-Q wavelet transform for classifying epileptic EEG signals by various researchers, and the publication of a volume of Pattern Recognit. Lett."},
