{"seizure__may_be_caused_by__conditions_such_as_epilepsy_a_high_fever_or_a_head_injury": "The phrase \"may be caused by\" indicates a potential cause-and-effect relationship, suggesting that certain conditions can lead to the occurrence of seizures."},
{"conditions_such_as_epilepsy_a_high_fever_or_a_head_injury": "Conditions such as epilepsy, a high fever, or a head injury are specific medical situations that can trigger seizures. Epilepsy is a neurological disorder marked by recurrent seizures, a high fever can disrupt normal brain function, and a head injury can damage brain tissue, all of which can result in seizure activity."},
