{"a_mechanism_of_pattern_recognition_unaffected_by_shift_in_position": "A mechanism of pattern recognition unaffected by shift in position refers to a system or method capable of identifying and categorizing patterns or objects within an image, regardless of their location or position within the visual field. This is a critical feature for robust pattern recognition systems, ensuring consistent performance across various input configurations."},
