{"k_c_chua": "K.C. Chua is a researcher and author with a focus on medical image analysis and biomedical engineering. His work includes the development of advanced computational and neural network techniques for segmenting eye structures in retinal images, analyzing electroencephalography (EEG) signals for epileptic identification, and exploring the use of ECG segments with convolutional neural networks for detecting coronary artery disease. He has collaborated with various researchers, including S.V. Bhandary, U.R. Acharya, V. Chandran, and C.M. Lim, on multiple research papers.|Here is another description: K.C. Chua is a researcher who has co-authored a paper with R.J. Martis on the application of empirical mode decomposition for automated detection of epilepsy using EEG signals. His expertise likely complements Martis's work in this domain."},
