{"automated_identification_of_epileptic_eeg_signals": "Automated identification of epileptic EEG signals refers to the process of using computational methods to detect and classify electroencephalogram (EEG) signals that are indicative of epileptic activity. This involves analyzing the patterns and characteristics of EEG data to distinguish between normal and abnormal (epileptic) signals without manual intervention."},
{"application_of_recurrence_quantification_analysis": "The application of recurrence quantification analysis refers to a specific method used for analyzing complex systems, particularly in the context of identifying patterns in time series data such as electroencephalogram (EEG) signals. This method is employed to automate the identification of epileptic EEG signals, enhancing the diagnostic process for epilepsy."},
